WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.604
A gift card is a code with money on it.

00:00:03.604 --> 00:00:07.829
This video shows how to sell gift cards, issue them by hand, follow

00:00:07.829 --> 00:00:12.285
and change each balance, how buyers pay with them at checkout, and what

00:00:12.285 --> 00:00:13.790
happens on a refund.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:22.487
A gift card is a gift that cannot be the wrong size or colour.

00:00:22.487 --> 00:00:25.921
For a store it is cash up front, and a reason for a

00:00:25.921 --> 00:00:27.970
friend to become a customer.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:33.548
Doing it by hand means codes in a spreadsheet, balances nobody trusts, and

00:00:33.548 --> 00:00:35.540
cards that are spent twice.

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:38.909
A gift card is a code with money on it.

00:00:38.909 --> 00:00:42.517
A buyer types it at checkout, it pays part or all of the

00:00:42.517 --> 00:00:45.310
order, and what is left stays on the card.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:49.977
You can sell gift cards like any product, and issue them by hand,

00:00:49.977 --> 00:00:52.680
for example to make up for a late delivery.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:57.961
Selling one:

00:00:57.961 --> 00:01:00.364
a gift card product holds a price.

00:01:00.364 --> 00:01:04.148
When an order for it is paid, one card for that amount is

00:01:04.148 --> 00:01:06.430
issued and emailed to the buyer.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:09.023
Issuing one by hand:

00:01:09.023 --> 00:01:15.120
enter an amount, a recipient and, if you like, your own code and an expiry date.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:16.958
Spending one:

00:01:16.958 --> 00:01:19.420
the buyer types the code at checkout.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:22.912
It pays like a second way to pay, and tax is worked out

00:01:22.912 --> 00:01:24.630
on the full price first.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:26.784
Following one:

00:01:26.784 --> 00:01:32.543
every card has a page with its balance and an activity list of every change.

00:01:32.543 --> 00:01:34.790
Open Commerce, Gift cards.

00:01:38.976 --> 00:01:43.321
Turning the feature on creates a Gift card content type.

00:01:43.321 --> 00:01:47.666
Open Content, Content Items, and create a new Gift card.

00:01:48.117 --> 00:01:53.029
Give it a title, such as Gift card 50 dollars, and a Price of 50.

00:01:53.029 --> 00:01:55.796
The price is what each card holds.

00:01:55.796 --> 00:01:59.877
Publish it, and it is ready to sell like any product.

00:02:00.328 --> 00:02:05.275
To show it in the shop, open Commerce, Product Listings, and edit the Shop.

00:02:05.275 --> 00:02:09.428
Under the product types it lists, tick Gift card, and publish.

00:02:13.622 --> 00:02:17.134
Open Commerce, Gift cards, and click Issue gift card.

00:02:17.134 --> 00:02:22.432
Enter the Amount, and check the Currency, which starts with your checkout currency.

00:02:22.884 --> 00:02:24.514
The Code is optional.

00:02:24.514 --> 00:02:29.222
Leave it blank to have an unguessable sixteen character code made up, or

00:02:29.222 --> 00:02:32.844
type your own, such as one printed on a physical card.

00:02:33.295 --> 00:02:37.890
Fill in the recipient's name and email, an optional expiry date, a message

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:41.509
for the email, and a note for the store only, such as why

00:02:41.509 --> 00:02:42.945
the card was given.

00:02:43.684 --> 00:02:46.677
Email the card sends the code to the recipient.

00:02:46.677 --> 00:02:50.234
Clear it to hand over the code yourself, and click Issue.

00:02:54.418 --> 00:02:58.885
The card's page shows its whole code, its balance, when it was issued,

00:02:58.885 --> 00:03:01.765
and for a bought card, a link to the order.

00:03:01.765 --> 00:03:06.290
You can change the recipient, the expiry and the note, or clear Enabled

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:09.758
to stop the card paying without changing its balance.

00:03:10.208 --> 00:03:15.583
Under Change the balance, enter an Amount and a Reason, and click Change balance.

00:03:15.583 --> 00:03:20.092
A positive amount adds to the card and a negative one takes off it.

00:03:20.092 --> 00:03:23.428
A reason is required, and is kept with the card.

00:03:23.879 --> 00:03:27.066
Activity lists every change, newest first:

00:03:27.066 --> 00:03:30.785
what it was, the change, and the balance after it.

00:03:30.785 --> 00:03:36.429
Under Email the card, Send emails the code again, for example when it was lost.

00:03:40.631 --> 00:03:45.466
Shoppers find a gift card in the shop and buy it like anything else.

00:03:45.466 --> 00:03:48.601
It is a digital product, so nothing ships.

00:03:49.054 --> 00:03:53.229
When the order is paid, one card is issued for each one bought,

00:03:53.229 --> 00:03:56.133
and it is emailed to the buyer to pass on.

00:03:56.133 --> 00:04:01.034
An order paid offline issues its cards turned off, until the money arrives.

00:04:05.212 --> 00:04:09.410
On the Payment step, the buyer types the code in the Gift card

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:11.077
box and clicks Apply.

00:04:11.077 --> 00:04:14.472
Dashes, spaces and capital letters do not matter.

00:04:14.922 --> 00:04:18.884
The box lists the card by its last four characters, what it pays,

00:04:18.884 --> 00:04:23.292
and what will be left on it, and the summary shows what is still due now.

00:04:23.292 --> 00:04:26.752
When cards pay everything, the button reads Place order.

00:04:27.204 --> 00:04:32.914
The order, its invoice and its confirmation email show Paid with gift card, and the amount.

00:04:37.105 --> 00:04:43.053
Commerce, Gift cards lists every card, newest first, with only the last four

00:04:43.053 --> 00:04:45.229
characters of each code.

00:04:45.229 --> 00:04:50.525
Search by code, its last four characters, or the recipient's email.

00:04:50.976 --> 00:04:52.558
Filter by status:

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:55.515
Active, Used up, Expired or Disabled.

00:04:55.515 --> 00:05:00.329
Each card shows its balance, when it expires, who it is for, and

00:05:00.329 --> 00:05:02.736
the order it was bought with.

00:05:03.186 --> 00:05:07.602
Open a card that was spent at checkout, and its activity shows what

00:05:07.602 --> 00:05:10.626
was spent, on which order, and what is left.

00:05:14.826 --> 00:05:18.729
Refunding an order paid with a gift card puts the money back on

00:05:18.729 --> 00:05:23.706
the card or wallet first, then on the gift card, and the card's activity shows it.

00:05:24.456 --> 00:05:28.818
Canceling or fully refunding an order that bought a card turns the card

00:05:28.818 --> 00:05:31.536
off, as long as nothing was spent from it.

00:05:32.286 --> 00:05:36.279
The money is held for a checkout while the buyer pays the rest,

00:05:36.279 --> 00:05:39.056
so two buyers cannot spend the same money.

00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:45.226
Codes avoid easy to misread characters, and trying many codes in a row is stopped.

00:05:49.426 --> 00:05:55.976
Sell cards in the amounts you choose, such as 25, 50 and 100, for the holidays.

00:05:56.726 --> 00:06:00.566
Make up for a late delivery with a card issued by hand.

00:06:01.316 --> 00:06:04.536
Print your own codes for a physical card in the shop.

00:06:05.286 --> 00:06:10.876
Give a prize or a loyalty reward, with an expiry date where the law allows one.

00:06:12.876 --> 00:06:18.449
Sell them, issue them, follow every balance, and let buyers spend them at checkout.

00:06:18.449 --> 00:06:20.076
Thanks for watching.

